  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Velocity of electron in $n^{\\text {th }}$ orbit of hydrogen atom is given by :\n$$\nV_n=\\frac{2 \\pi K Z e^2}{n h}\n$$\nSubstituting the values we get,\n$$\nV_n=\\frac{2.2 \\times 10^6}{n} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s} \\quad \\text { or } \\quad V_n \\propto \\frac{1}{n}\n$$\nAs principal quantum number increases, velocity decreases.",
    "image": null
